            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56363",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56363"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56363?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u12",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick before 7.1.2-22 contains a division by zero vulnerability in binomial kernel processing that allows attackers to cause denial of service. An attacker can supply a large binomial kernel value causing integer overflow, resulting in division by zero and application crash.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.23+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-vf33-6r7x-66xx\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/d67eef71764cfeca07b4edf8a8ae922180f5f2e4 (7.1.2-22)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/7a48e0b3107608c7d87a172473cfd5294bc9e81f (6.9.13-47)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick before 7.1.2-22 contains a division by zero vulnerability in binomial kernel processing that allows attackers to cause denial of service. An attacker can supply a large binomial kernel value causing integer overflow, resulting in division by zero and application crash.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.23+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-vf33-6r7x-66xx\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/d67eef71764cfeca07b4edf8a8ae922180f5f2e4 (7.1.2-22)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/7a48e0b3107608c7d87a172473cfd5294bc9e81f (6.9.13-47)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u12                                                                                |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u12                                                                                 |\n"
