            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57432",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57432"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-57432?s=debian&n=perl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.10 have an integer overflow in S_measure_struct leading to an out-of-bounds heap read in pack and unpack.  S_measure_struct adds each item's size times its repeat count to a running total with no overflow check, so a large repeat count in a pack or unpack template wraps the signed SSize_t total negative. The @, X, and x position codes then guard their moves with a signed length comparison that passes when the length is negative, advancing the buffer pointer out of bounds.  A template derived from untrusted input can read heap memory past the buffer and return it to the caller.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138905; bug #1142036)\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780102/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/5f7eb6bbbe0510964e3fb1d6bb691e5445913e55 (v5.43.11)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/40754edc72dd3e513d758153c0e2f0215897740e (v5.43.11)\n",
                "markdown": "> Perl versions through 5.43.10 have an integer overflow in S_measure_struct leading to an out-of-bounds heap read in pack and unpack.  S_measure_struct adds each item's size times its repeat count to a running total with no overflow check, so a large repeat count in a pack or unpack template wraps the signed SSize_t total negative. The @, X, and x position codes then guard their moves with a signed length comparison that passes when the length is negative, advancing the buffer pointer out of bounds.  A template derived from untrusted input can read heap memory past the buffer and return it to the caller.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138905; bug #1142036)\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780102/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/5f7eb6bbbe0510964e3fb1d6bb691e5445913e55 (v5.43.11)\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/40754edc72dd3e513d758153c0e2f0215897740e (v5.43.11)\n\n|                |                                                                                        |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                     |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                              |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57433",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57433"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-57433?s=debian&n=perl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.  retrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.  A crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138906; bug #1142035)\n- libstorable-perl <removed>\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780100/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/e4f681784bcdeaa91ff02a2fa4cdcae5c46779d7 (v5.43.11)\n",
                "markdown": "> Storable versions before 3.41 for Perl have a signed integer overflow when deserializing a crafted SX_HOOK record.  retrieve_hook_common reads a signed 32-bit item count from an SX_HOOK record and calls av_extend with that count plus one. A count of I32_MAX wraps the addition to a negative value.  A crafted blob passed to thaw or retrieve triggers the overflow; av_extend receives the negative count and dies with a panic, terminating the deserialization.\n\n---\n- perl 5.40.1-8 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1138906; bug #1142035)\n- libstorable-perl <removed>\nhttps://lists.security.metacpan.org/cve-announce/msg/41780100/\nFixed by: https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/e4f681784bcdeaa91ff02a2fa4cdcae5c46779d7 (v5.43.11)\n\n|                |                                                                                        |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                     |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                              |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl@5.36.0-7%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58050",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-58050"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-58050?s=debian&n=libssh2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1 reads an attacker-controlled 32-bit attribute count from a publickey-subsystem response and uses it in the allocation num_attrs * sizeof(libssh2_publickey_attribute) without bounds checking, so on 32-bit platforms the multiplication overflows to an undersized buffer. A malicious SSH server can then drive the attribute-parsing loop to write past the allocation, causing a heap buffer overflow in a connecting libssh2 client.\n\n---\n- libssh2 1.11.1-6 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144415)\n[trixie] - libssh2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue; can be fixed via point release)\nhttps://github.com/bikini/exploitarium/tree/main/libssh2-publickey-list-calc-poc\nhttps://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2128\nFixed by: https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/34497525929b9a47f03dfb81887ac896202b7e12\n",
                "markdown": "> libssh2 through 1.11.1 reads an attacker-controlled 32-bit attribute count from a publickey-subsystem response and uses it in the allocation num_attrs * sizeof(libssh2_publickey_attribute) without bounds checking, so on 32-bit platforms the multiplication overflows to an undersized buffer. A malicious SSH server can then drive the attribute-parsing loop to write past the allocation, causing a heap buffer overflow in a connecting libssh2 client.\n\n---\n- libssh2 1.11.1-6 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144415)\n[trixie] - libssh2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue; can be fixed via point release)\nhttps://github.com/bikini/exploitarium/tree/main/libssh2-publickey-list-calc-poc\nhttps://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2128\nFixed by: https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/34497525929b9a47f03dfb81887ac896202b7e12\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libssh2@1.10.0-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                              |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2@1.10.0-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58051",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-58051"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-58051?s=debian&n=libssh2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1 grows its publickey list with SSH2_REALLOC but does not zero-initialize new entries before parsing populates them, so a parse failure reaching the cleanup path leaves libssh2_publickey_list_free operating on an uninitialized entry. A malicious SSH server offering the publickey subsystem can use a malformed response to make cleanup free an uninitialized, attacker-influenceable attrs pointer in a connecting libssh2 client.\n\n---\n- libssh2 1.11.1-6 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144415)\n[trixie] - libssh2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue; can be fixed via point release)\nhttps://github.com/bikini/exploitarium/tree/main/libssh2-publickey-list-calc-poc\nhttps://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2127\nFixed by: https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/a9758da45a52bc8c630ec9493804d0c6ea30b24a\n",
                "markdown": "> libssh2 through 1.11.1 grows its publickey list with SSH2_REALLOC but does not zero-initialize new entries before parsing populates them, so a parse failure reaching the cleanup path leaves libssh2_publickey_list_free operating on an uninitialized entry. A malicious SSH server offering the publickey subsystem can use a malformed response to make cleanup free an uninitialized, attacker-influenceable attrs pointer in a connecting libssh2 client.\n\n---\n- libssh2 1.11.1-6 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144415)\n[trixie] - libssh2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue; can be fixed via point release)\nhttps://github.com/bikini/exploitarium/tree/main/libssh2-publickey-list-calc-poc\nhttps://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2127\nFixed by: https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/a9758da45a52bc8c630ec9493804d0c6ea30b24a\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libssh2@1.10.0-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                              |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "UNSPECIFIED",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2@1.10.0-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "UNSPECIFIED"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-61464",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
