              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2007-2768?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "OpenSSH, when using OPIE (One-Time Passwords in Everything) for PAM, allows remote attackers to determine the existence of certain user accounts, which displays a different response if the user account exists and is configured to use one-time passwords (OTP), a similar issue to CVE-2007-2243.\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=436571; unimportant)\n[etch] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[sarge] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttp://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=112279\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenSSH, when using OPIE (One-Time Passwords in Everything) for PAM, allows remote attackers to determine the existence of certain user accounts, which displays a different response if the user account exists and is configured to use one-time passwords (OTP), a similar issue to CVE-2007-2243.\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=436571; unimportant)\n[etch] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[sarge] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttp://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=112279\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                    |\n"
