            {
              "id": "CVE-2007-3476",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2007-3476"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2007-3476?s=debian&n=libwmf&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Array index error in gd_gif_in.c in the GD Graphics Library (libgd) before 2.0.35 allows user-assisted remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash and heap corruption) via large color index values in crafted image data, which results in a segmentation fault.\n\n---\n- libgd2 2.0.35.dfsg-1 (low)\n- libwmf <unfixed> (unimportant)\n- racket 5.0.2-1 (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=601525)\nOnly present in one of the sample pl-scheme packages (plot)\ncan write a 0 to a 4k window in heap, very unlikely to be controllable.\n",
                "markdown": "> Array index error in gd_gif_in.c in the GD Graphics Library (libgd) before 2.0.35 allows user-assisted remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash and heap corruption) via large color index values in crafted image data, which results in a segmentation fault.\n\n---\n- libgd2 2.0.35.dfsg-1 (low)\n- libwmf <unfixed> (unimportant)\n- racket 5.0.2-1 (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=601525)\nOnly present in one of the sample pl-scheme packages (plot)\ncan write a 0 to a 4k window in heap, very unlikely to be controllable.\n\n|                |                                                                                  |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libwmf@0.2.12-5.1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                        |\n"
              },
