            {
              "id": "CVE-2008-1687",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2008-1687"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2008-1687?s=debian&n=m4&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The (1) maketemp and (2) mkstemp builtin functions in GNU m4 before 1.4.11 do not quote their output when a file is created, which might allow context-dependent attackers to trigger a macro expansion, leading to unspecified use of an incorrect filename.\n\n---\n- m4 <unfixed> (unimportant)\nThis is more a generic bug and not a security issue: the random output would\nneed to match the name of an existing macro\n",
                "markdown": "> The (1) maketemp and (2) mkstemp builtin functions in GNU m4 before 1.4.11 do not quote their output when a file is created, which might allow context-dependent attackers to trigger a macro expansion, leading to unspecified use of an incorrect filename.\n\n---\n- m4 <unfixed> (unimportant)\nThis is more a generic bug and not a security issue: the random output would\nneed to match the name of an existing macro\n\n|                |                                                                            |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/m4@1.4.19-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
