            {
              "id": "CVE-2008-1688",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2008-1688"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2008-1688?s=debian&n=m4&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Unspecified vulnerability in GNU m4 before 1.4.11 might allow context-dependent attackers to execute arbitrary code, related to improper handling of filenames specified with the -F option.  NOTE: it is not clear when this issue crosses privilege boundaries.\n\n---\n- m4 <unfixed> (unimportant)\nThe file name is passed through a cmdline argument and m4 doesn't run with\nelevated privileges.\n",
                "markdown": "> Unspecified vulnerability in GNU m4 before 1.4.11 might allow context-dependent attackers to execute arbitrary code, related to improper handling of filenames specified with the -F option.  NOTE: it is not clear when this issue crosses privilege boundaries.\n\n---\n- m4 <unfixed> (unimportant)\nThe file name is passed through a cmdline argument and m4 doesn't run with\nelevated privileges.\n\n|                |                                                                            |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/m4@1.4.19-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                  |\n"
