              "help": {
                "text": "sshd in OpenSSH 4 on Debian GNU/Linux, and the 20070303 OpenSSH snapshot, allows remote authenticated users to obtain access to arbitrary SELinux roles by appending a :/ (colon slash) sequence, followed by the role name, to the username.\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (unimportant)\nthis is by design\n",
