            {
              "id": "CVE-2010-4651",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2010-4651"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2010-4651?s=debian&n=patch&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Directory traversal vulnerability in util.c in GNU patch 2.6.1 and earlier allows user-assisted remote attackers to create or overwrite arbitrary files via a filename that is specified with a .. (dot dot) or full pathname, a related issue to CVE-2010-1679.\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nApplying a patch blindly opens more severe security issues than only directory traversal...\nopenwall ships a fix\nSee https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=667529 for details\n",
                "markdown": "> Directory traversal vulnerability in util.c in GNU patch 2.6.1 and earlier allows user-assisted remote attackers to create or overwrite arbitrary files via a filename that is specified with a .. (dot dot) or full pathname, a related issue to CVE-2010-1679.\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nApplying a patch blindly opens more severe security issues than only directory traversal...\nopenwall ships a fix\nSee https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=667529 for details\n\n|                |                                                                              |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                    |\n"
