              "help": {
                "text": "OpenSSH through 8.7 allows remote attackers, who have a suspicion that a certain combination of username and public key is known to an SSH server, to test whether this suspicion is correct. This occurs because a challenge is sent only when that combination could be valid for a login session. NOTE: the vendor does not recognize user enumeration as a vulnerability for this product\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/pull/270\nNegligible impact, not treated as a security issue by upstream\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenSSH through 8.7 allows remote attackers, who have a suspicion that a certain combination of username and public key is known to an SSH server, to test whether this suspicion is correct. This occurs because a challenge is sent only when that combination could be valid for a login session. NOTE: the vendor does not recognize user enumeration as a vulnerability for this product\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/pull/270\nNegligible impact, not treated as a security issue by upstream\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                    |\n"
