            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-16232",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-16232"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2017-16232?s=debian&n=tiff&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "LibTIFF 4.0.8 has multiple memory leak vulnerabilities, which allow attackers to cause a denial of service (memory consumption), as demonstrated by tif_open.c, tif_lzw.c, and tif_aux.c. NOTE: Third parties were unable to reproduce the issue\n\n---\n- tiff <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttp://seclists.org/oss-sec/2017/q4/168\nRelated commit: https://gitlab.com/libtiff/libtiff/commit/25f9ffa56548c1846c4a1f19308b7f561f7b1ab0\nThis is actually only a partial fix, but upstream will not fix it completely.\nThe related commit is included in 4.0.9. The underlying memory-based DOS\nwould still be present.\n",
                "markdown": "> LibTIFF 4.0.8 has multiple memory leak vulnerabilities, which allow attackers to cause a denial of service (memory consumption), as demonstrated by tif_open.c, tif_lzw.c, and tif_aux.c. NOTE: Third parties were unable to reproduce the issue\n\n---\n- tiff <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttp://seclists.org/oss-sec/2017/q4/168\nRelated commit: https://gitlab.com/libtiff/libtiff/commit/25f9ffa56548c1846c4a1f19308b7f561f7b1ab0\nThis is actually only a partial fix, but upstream will not fix it completely.\nThe related commit is included in 4.0.9. The underlying memory-based DOS\nwould still be present.\n\n|                |                                                                                       |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/tiff@4.5.0-6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                    |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                             |\n"
              },
