                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.1-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-7275",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-7275"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2017-7275?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The ReadPCXImage function in coders/pcx.c in ImageMagick 7.0.4.9 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (attempted large memory allocation and application crash) via a crafted file. NOTE: this vulnerability exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2016-8862 and CVE-2016-8866.\n\n---\n- imagemagick <unfixed> (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=859025)\nhttps://blogs.gentoo.org/ago/2017/03/27/imagemagick-memory-allocation-failure-in-acquiremagickmemory-memory-c-incomplete-fix-for-cve-2016-8862-and-cve-2016-8866/\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/issues/271\nFurthermore: upstream is not able to reproduce the problem as well\nThe problem result in a memory allocation issue when compiled with ASAN\nbut unreproducible from unstream. Since no more details can be provided\nand the issue not addressed, treat this as \"non-issue\" (and thus marked\nunimportant). If in future details can be elaborated by the reporter\nwe might re-evaluate this entry.\n",
                "markdown": "> The ReadPCXImage function in coders/pcx.c in ImageMagick 7.0.4.9 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (attempted large memory allocation and application crash) via a crafted file. NOTE: this vulnerability exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2016-8862 and CVE-2016-8866.\n\n---\n- imagemagick <unfixed> (unimportant; bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=859025)\nhttps://blogs.gentoo.org/ago/2017/03/27/imagemagick-memory-allocation-failure-in-acquiremagickmemory-memory-c-incomplete-fix-for-cve-2016-8862-and-cve-2016-8866/\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/issues/271\nFurthermore: upstream is not able to reproduce the problem as well\nThe problem result in a memory allocation issue when compiled with ASAN\nbut unreproducible from unstream. Since no more details can be provided\nand the issue not addressed, treat this as \"non-issue\" (and thus marked\nunimportant). If in future details can be elaborated by the reporter\nwe might re-evaluate this entry.\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                                            |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                                     |\n"
              },
