              "help": {
                "text": "The demangle_template function in cplus-dem.c in GNU libiberty, as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.31.1, contains an integer overflow vulnerability (for \"Create an array for saving the template argument values\") that can trigger a heap-based buffer overflow, as demonstrated by nm.\n\n---\n- binutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=24039\nbinutils not covered by security support\n",
                "markdown": "> The demangle_template function in cplus-dem.c in GNU libiberty, as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.31.1, contains an integer overflow vulnerability (for \"Create an array for saving the template argument values\") that can trigger a heap-based buffer overflow, as demonstrated by nm.\n\n---\n- binutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=24039\nbinutils not covered by security support\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/binutils@2.40-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
