              "help": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in GNU patch through 2.7.6. There is a segmentation fault, associated with a NULL pointer dereference, leading to a denial of service in the intuit_diff_type function in pch.c, aka a \"mangled rename\" issue.\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=f290f48a621867084884bfff87f8093c15195e6a\nhttps://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53132\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> An issue was discovered in GNU patch through 2.7.6. There is a segmentation fault, associated with a NULL pointer dereference, leading to a denial of service in the intuit_diff_type function in pch.c, aka a \"mangled rename\" issue.\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=f290f48a621867084884bfff87f8093c15195e6a\nhttps://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53132\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n\n|                |                                                                              |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                    |\n"
              },
