                "text": "A vulnerability classified as problematic was found in LibTIFF 4.3.0. Affected by this vulnerability is the TIFF File Handler of tiff2ps. Opening a malicious file leads to a denial of service. The attack can be launched remotely but requires user interaction. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used.\n\n---\n- tiff <unfixed> (unimportant)\n[bullseye] - tiff <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[buster] - tiff <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://gitlab.com/libtiff/libtiff/-/issues/402\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> A vulnerability classified as problematic was found in LibTIFF 4.3.0. Affected by this vulnerability is the TIFF File Handler of tiff2ps. Opening a malicious file leads to a denial of service. The attack can be launched remotely but requires user interaction. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used.\n\n---\n- tiff <unfixed> (unimportant)\n[bullseye] - tiff <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[buster] - tiff <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://gitlab.com/libtiff/libtiff/-/issues/402\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n\n|                |                                                                                       |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/tiff@4.5.0-6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                    |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                             |\n"
