            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4516",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4516"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4516?s=debian&n=python3.11&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C3.11.2-6%2Bdeb12u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "There is an issue in CPython when using `bytes.decode(\"unicode_escape\", error=\"ignore|replace\")`. If you are not using the \"unicode_escape\" encoding or an error handler your usage is not affected. To work-around this issue you may stop using the error= handler and instead wrap the bytes.decode() call in a try-except catching the DecodeError.\n\n---\n- python3.13 3.13.3-4\n- python3.12 <removed>\n- python3.11 <removed>\n[bookworm] - python3.11 3.11.2-6+deb12u7\n- python3.9 <removed>\n- pypy3 <not-affected> (Vulnerable code not present; memory error in C code implementation)\nhttps://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/L75IPBBTSCYEF56I2M4KIW353BB3AY74/\nPoC: https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/05/19/1\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/133767\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/129648\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/9f69a58623bd01349a18ba0c7a9cb1dad6a51e8e (main)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/69b4387f78f413e8c47572a85b3478c47eba8142 (v3.14.0b2)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/6279eb8c076d89d3739a6edb393e43c7929b429d (v3.13.4)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/73b3040f592436385007918887b7e2132aa8431f (v3.11.13)\n",
                "markdown": "> There is an issue in CPython when using `bytes.decode(\"unicode_escape\", error=\"ignore|replace\")`. If you are not using the \"unicode_escape\" encoding or an error handler your usage is not affected. To work-around this issue you may stop using the error= handler and instead wrap the bytes.decode() call in a try-except catching the DecodeError.\n\n---\n- python3.13 3.13.3-4\n- python3.12 <removed>\n- python3.11 <removed>\n[bookworm] - python3.11 3.11.2-6+deb12u7\n- python3.9 <removed>\n- pypy3 <not-affected> (Vulnerable code not present; memory error in C code implementation)\nhttps://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/L75IPBBTSCYEF56I2M4KIW353BB3AY74/\nPoC: https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/05/19/1\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/133767\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/129648\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/9f69a58623bd01349a18ba0c7a9cb1dad6a51e8e (main)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/69b4387f78f413e8c47572a85b3478c47eba8142 (v3.14.0b2)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/6279eb8c076d89d3739a6edb393e43c7929b429d (v3.13.4)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/73b3040f592436385007918887b7e2132aa8431f (v3.11.13)\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/python3.11@3.11.2-6%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <3.11.2-6+deb12u7                                                                            |\n| Fixed version  | 3.11.2-6+deb12u7                                                                             |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<3.11.2-6+deb12u7",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "3.11.2-6+deb12u7",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/python3.11@3.11.2-6%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
