            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3949",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-3949"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-3949?s=debian&n=libheif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was determined in strukturag libheif up to 1.21.2. This affects the function vvdec_push_data2 of the file libheif/plugins/decoder_vvdec.cc of the component HEIF File Parser. Executing a manipulation of the argument size can lead to out-of-bounds read. The attack needs to be launched locally. The exploit has been publicly disclosed and may be utilized. This patch is called b97c8b5f198b27f375127cd597a35f2113544d03. It is advisable to implement a patch to correct this issue.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/issues/1712\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/b97c8b5f198b27f375127cd597a35f2113544d03 (v1.22.0)\nThe 'vvdec' backend is not built for the Debian binary packages\n",
                "markdown": "> A vulnerability was determined in strukturag libheif up to 1.21.2. This affects the function vvdec_push_data2 of the file libheif/plugins/decoder_vvdec.cc of the component HEIF File Parser. Executing a manipulation of the argument size can lead to out-of-bounds read. The attack needs to be launched locally. The exploit has been publicly disclosed and may be utilized. This patch is called b97c8b5f198b27f375127cd597a35f2113544d03. It is advisable to implement a patch to correct this issue.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (unimportant)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/issues/1712\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/b97c8b5f198b27f375127cd597a35f2113544d03 (v1.22.0)\nThe 'vvdec' backend is not built for the Debian binary packages\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                        |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41069",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41069"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-41069?s=debian&n=libheif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. In versions 1.21.2 and prior, a malformed HEIF sequence file can trigger an out-of-bounds read in core sequence parsing logic, causing DoS. A malformed file can have stco.entry_count == 0 (creating no chunks) while still passing validation because saio.entry_count == 0 matches, but with saiz.sample_count > 0 the SampleAuxInfoReader constructor still enters its loop. This leads to an out-of-bounds dereference on the empty chunks[0] in chunked mode.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1137524)\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-p82x-fpmv-576r\n",
                "markdown": "> libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. In versions 1.21.2 and prior, a malformed HEIF sequence file can trigger an out-of-bounds read in core sequence parsing logic, causing DoS. A malformed file can have stco.entry_count == 0 (creating no chunks) while still passing validation because saio.entry_count == 0 matches, but with saiz.sample_count > 0 the SampleAuxInfoReader constructor still enters its loop. This leads to an out-of-bounds dereference on the empty chunks[0] in chunked mode.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1137524)\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-p82x-fpmv-576r\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                        |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41071",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41071"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-41071?s=debian&n=libheif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. In versions 1.21.2 and prior, a crafted HEIF sequence file where the saiz box declares more samples than actually exist in the track's chunk table causes a heap-buffer-overflow (out-of-bounds read) in the SampleAuxInfoReader constructor. The SampleAuxInfoReader constructor iterates over saiz->get_num_samples() samples but doesn't validate that this count is consistent with the number of chunks in the chunks vector. When saiz declares more samples than the chunks cover, the loop increments current_chunk past chunks.size(), causing an out-of-bounds read on the chunks vector. The vulnerability is triggered during file parsing (heif_context_read_from_file) without any additional user interaction. Any application using libheif to open untrusted HEIF files is affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.22.0.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1137524)\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-xj92-xjff-h8w3\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/f20c81745e917b4c496615140385c86d7a2fa58d (v1.22.0)\n",
                "markdown": "> libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. In versions 1.21.2 and prior, a crafted HEIF sequence file where the saiz box declares more samples than actually exist in the track's chunk table causes a heap-buffer-overflow (out-of-bounds read) in the SampleAuxInfoReader constructor. The SampleAuxInfoReader constructor iterates over saiz->get_num_samples() samples but doesn't validate that this count is consistent with the number of chunks in the chunks vector. When saiz declares more samples than the chunks cover, the loop increments current_chunk past chunks.size(), causing an out-of-bounds read on the chunks vector. The vulnerability is triggered during file parsing (heif_context_read_from_file) without any additional user interaction. Any application using libheif to open untrusted HEIF files is affected. This issue has been fixed in version 1.22.0.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1137524)\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-xj92-xjff-h8w3\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/f20c81745e917b4c496615140385c86d7a2fa58d (v1.22.0)\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                        |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41989",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41989"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-41989?s=debian&n=libgcrypt20&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1.10.1-3%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Libgcrypt before 1.12.2 sometimes allows a heap-based buffer overflow and denial of service via crafted ECDH ciphertext to gcry_pk_decrypt.\n\n---\n- libgcrypt20 1.12.2-1\n[bullseye] - libgcrypt20 <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced later)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/21/1\nhttps://dev.gnupg.org/T8211\nFixed by: https://git.gnupg.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=libgcrypt.git;a=commit;h=2d3d732c9bf87cc10729f69678dd9e6862f99fa3 (libgcrypt-1.12.2)\nIntroduced by: https://git.gnupg.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=libgcrypt.git;a=commit;h=bbe15758c893dbf546416c1a6bccdad1ab000ad7 (libgcrypt-1.9.0)\n",
                "markdown": "> Libgcrypt before 1.12.2 sometimes allows a heap-based buffer overflow and denial of service via crafted ECDH ciphertext to gcry_pk_decrypt.\n\n---\n- libgcrypt20 1.12.2-1\n[bullseye] - libgcrypt20 <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced later)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/21/1\nhttps://dev.gnupg.org/T8211\nFixed by: https://git.gnupg.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=libgcrypt.git;a=commit;h=2d3d732c9bf87cc10729f69678dd9e6862f99fa3 (libgcrypt-1.12.2)\nIntroduced by: https://git.gnupg.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=libgcrypt.git;a=commit;h=bbe15758c893dbf546416c1a6bccdad1ab000ad7 (libgcrypt-1.9.0)\n\n|                |                                                                                     |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libgcrypt20@1.10.1-3?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1.10.1-3+deb12u1                                                                   |\n| Fixed version  | 1.10.1-3+deb12u1                                                                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.10.1-3+deb12u1",
