            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-47254",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-47254"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-47254?s=debian&n=libheif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. Prior to version 1.22.0, `Track::init_sample_timing_table()` in `libheif/sequences/track.cc` stores an out-of-bounds chunk index (`m_chunks.size()`) into `m_presentation_timeline` when the number of chunks defined in the `stco` box is less than the number of samples in `stsz`. A subsequent call to `heif_track_get_next_raw_sequence_sample()` reads `m_chunks[chunk_idx]` with that OOB index, causing a heap-buffer-overflow. Version 1.22.0 fixes the issue.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-wqjg-4x9g-6cvg\n",
                "markdown": "> libheif is a HEIF and AVIF file format decoder and encoder. Prior to version 1.22.0, `Track::init_sample_timing_table()` in `libheif/sequences/track.cc` stores an out-of-bounds chunk index (`m_chunks.size()`) into `m_presentation_timeline` when the number of chunks defined in the `stco` box is less than the number of samples in `stsz`. A subsequent call to `heif_track_get_next_raw_sequence_sample()` reads `m_chunks[chunk_idx]` with that OOB index, causing a heap-buffer-overflow. Version 1.22.0 fixes the issue.\n\n---\n- libheif 1.23.1-1\n[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Vulnerable code introduced in 1.20.0)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-wqjg-4x9g-6cvg\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                        |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
