            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56210",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56210"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56210?s=debian&n=aom&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A heap-buffer-overflow read vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference AV1 codec implementation. A missing bounds check in the SVC (Scalable Video Coding) layer ID control function allows setting a spatial_layer_id exceeding the configured number of layers. This causes an out-of-bounds heap read of approximately 40,728 bytes when computing a layer context array index. An attacker who can influence SVC encoder parameters in a network-facing service could exploit this for information disclosure (heap content leak) or denial of service (segmentation fault from hitting unmapped memory).\n\n---\n- aom 3.14.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1140428)\n[bullseye] - aom <not-affected> (1.0.0 lacks the SVC encoder layer_context array, introduced in 2.0.0)\nhttps://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/a93ba0ffaacd5f576a241bf739110e65287e516d\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2490801\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues/503975732\n",
                "markdown": "> A heap-buffer-overflow read vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference AV1 codec implementation. A missing bounds check in the SVC (Scalable Video Coding) layer ID control function allows setting a spatial_layer_id exceeding the configured number of layers. This causes an out-of-bounds heap read of approximately 40,728 bytes when computing a layer context array index. An attacker who can influence SVC encoder parameters in a network-facing service could exploit this for information disclosure (heap content leak) or denial of service (segmentation fault from hitting unmapped memory).\n\n---\n- aom 3.14.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1140428)\n[bullseye] - aom <not-affected> (1.0.0 lacks the SVC encoder layer_context array, introduced in 2.0.0)\nhttps://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/a93ba0ffaacd5f576a241bf739110e65287e516d\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2490801\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues/503975732\n\n|                |                                                                                      |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/aom@3.6.0-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                   |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                            |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/aom@3.6.0-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56211",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56211"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56211?s=debian&n=aom&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A remote code execution vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference AV1 codec implementation. Insufficient bounds validation in the AV1 encoder's SVC (Scalable Video Coding) layer ID control allows an attacker to supply crafted video frame pixels that overlap with internal encoder layer context structures. In fork-based video processing services, an attacker can use this to hijack the cyclic refresh map pointer, brute-force the process base address via a crash oracle, and redirect control flow to achieve arbitrary command execution. Exploitation requires the target service to use libaom with SVC encoding enabled and accept attacker-supplied video frames.\n\n---\n- aom 3.14.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1140428)\n[bullseye] - aom <not-affected> (1.0.0 lacks the aom_svc_layer_id_t encoder control, introduced in 2.0.0)\nhttps://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/a93ba0ffaacd5f576a241bf739110e65287e516d\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2490802\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues/503993985\n",
                "markdown": "> A remote code execution vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference AV1 codec implementation. Insufficient bounds validation in the AV1 encoder's SVC (Scalable Video Coding) layer ID control allows an attacker to supply crafted video frame pixels that overlap with internal encoder layer context structures. In fork-based video processing services, an attacker can use this to hijack the cyclic refresh map pointer, brute-force the process base address via a crash oracle, and redirect control flow to achieve arbitrary command execution. Exploitation requires the target service to use libaom with SVC encoding enabled and accept attacker-supplied video frames.\n\n---\n- aom 3.14.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1140428)\n[bullseye] - aom <not-affected> (1.0.0 lacks the aom_svc_layer_id_t encoder control, introduced in 2.0.0)\nhttps://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/a93ba0ffaacd5f576a241bf739110e65287e516d\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2490802\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues/503993985\n\n|                |                                                                                      |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/aom@3.6.0-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                   |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                            |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/aom@3.6.0-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56288",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56288"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56288?s=debian&n=patch&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU patch is vulnerable to a NULL pointer dereference when processing a specially crafted unified-diff patch file. Improper handling of consecutive end-of-file newline markers can corrupt internal hunk (single block of changes in diff) data structures, causing the application to pass a NULL pointer to fwrite() during patch processing. An attacker can trigger this condition with a malicious patch file, causing the utility to crash and resulting in a denial of service.    This issue has been fixed in the commit e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/07/CVE-2026-56288/\nhttps://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU patch is vulnerable to a NULL pointer dereference when processing a specially crafted unified-diff patch file. Improper handling of consecutive end-of-file newline markers can corrupt internal hunk (single block of changes in diff) data structures, causing the application to pass a NULL pointer to fwrite() during patch processing. An attacker can trigger this condition with a malicious patch file, causing the utility to crash and resulting in a denial of service.    This issue has been fixed in the commit e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/07/CVE-2026-56288/\nhttps://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=e6d6a4e021660679d7fc9150f981d4920f722313\nCrash in CLI tool, no security impact\n\n|                |                                                                              |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56289",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56289"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56289?s=debian&n=patch&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU patch is vulnerable to a denial of service (DoS) due to improper validation of hunk (single block of changes in diff) line offsets in unified-diff input. A specially crafted patch can specify an extremely large line number, causing the application to enter an effectively infinite processing loop while attempting to locate the requested position. This results in excessive CPU consumption and prevents the process from completing. An attacker can trigger this behavior by supplying a malicious patch file, causing the utility to become unresponsive and require manual termination.    This issue has been fixed in the commit faba04ef4f2b410257f76c1b9dc85e350929c4b9\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/07/CVE-2026-56288/\nhttps://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=faba04ef4f2b410257f76c1b9dc85e350929c4b9\nHang in CLI tool, no security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU patch is vulnerable to a denial of service (DoS) due to improper validation of hunk (single block of changes in diff) line offsets in unified-diff input. A specially crafted patch can specify an extremely large line number, causing the application to enter an effectively infinite processing loop while attempting to locate the requested position. This results in excessive CPU consumption and prevents the process from completing. An attacker can trigger this behavior by supplying a malicious patch file, causing the utility to become unresponsive and require manual termination.    This issue has been fixed in the commit faba04ef4f2b410257f76c1b9dc85e350929c4b9\n\n---\n- patch <unfixed> (unimportant)\nhttps://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/07/CVE-2026-56288/\nhttps://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/patch.git/commit/?id=faba04ef4f2b410257f76c1b9dc85e350929c4b9\nHang in CLI tool, no security impact\n\n|                |                                                                              |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/patch@2.7.6-7?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56391",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56391"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56391?s=debian&n=coreutils&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU coreutils uniq is vulnerable to an out‑of‑bounds read due to incorrect handling of multibyte input when the -w (--check-chars) option is used. The find_field() function miscalculates the byte length of characters by repeatedly processing a fixed pointer instead of advancing through the input, resulting in an inflated length value.  This incorrect length is later used in a memcmp operation, causing reads beyond the allocated buffer when processing crafted multibyte input.  When running GNU coreutils uniq with attacker-provided arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potential adjacent heap memory exposure.   This issue has been fixed in the commit d64e35a8a4c0e4608321433e0d84d917e4e36371.\n\n---\n- coreutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nFixed by: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/coreutils.git/commit/?id=d64e35a8a4c0e4608321433e0d84d917e4e36371\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/07/25/2\nNegligible security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU coreutils uniq is vulnerable to an out‑of‑bounds read due to incorrect handling of multibyte input when the -w (--check-chars) option is used. The find_field() function miscalculates the byte length of characters by repeatedly processing a fixed pointer instead of advancing through the input, resulting in an inflated length value.  This incorrect length is later used in a memcmp operation, causing reads beyond the allocated buffer when processing crafted multibyte input.  When running GNU coreutils uniq with attacker-provided arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potential adjacent heap memory exposure.   This issue has been fixed in the commit d64e35a8a4c0e4608321433e0d84d917e4e36371.\n\n---\n- coreutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nFixed by: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/coreutils.git/commit/?id=d64e35a8a4c0e4608321433e0d84d917e4e36371\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/07/25/2\nNegligible security impact\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.1-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.1-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56392",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56392"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56392?s=debian&n=coreutils&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU coreutils unexpand is vulnerable to a heap-based buffer overflow due to an integer overflow during buffer allocation when processing large tab stop (-t) values. The multiplication used to calculate the allocation size can wrap around, resulting in an undersized buffer. When processing crafted input, subsequent writes exceed the allocated memory, leading to an out‑of‑bounds heap write.  When running GNU coreutils unexpand with attacker-provided large tab stop (-t) arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potentially achieve a heap write primitive depending on memory layout.           This issue has been fixed in the commit b60a159fdc5bfcf9988d3a4cb6f53abe8ad5d35d\n\n---\n- coreutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nFixed by: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/coreutils.git/commit/?id=b60a159fdc5bfcf9988d3a4cb6f53abe8ad5d35d\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/07/25/2\nNegligible security impact\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU coreutils unexpand is vulnerable to a heap-based buffer overflow due to an integer overflow during buffer allocation when processing large tab stop (-t) values. The multiplication used to calculate the allocation size can wrap around, resulting in an undersized buffer. When processing crafted input, subsequent writes exceed the allocated memory, leading to an out‑of‑bounds heap write.  When running GNU coreutils unexpand with attacker-provided large tab stop (-t) arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potentially achieve a heap write primitive depending on memory layout.           This issue has been fixed in the commit b60a159fdc5bfcf9988d3a4cb6f53abe8ad5d35d\n\n---\n- coreutils <unfixed> (unimportant)\nFixed by: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/coreutils.git/commit/?id=b60a159fdc5bfcf9988d3a4cb6f53abe8ad5d35d\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/07/25/2\nNegligible security impact\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.1-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
