            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15310",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15310"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-15310?s=debian&n=python3.11&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "When decompressing crafted zip files using the bzip/LZMA/Zstandard   compressions, Python could use an attacker-controlled size to   pre-allocate memory, possibly resulting in memory exhaustion.\n\n---\n- python3.15 <unfixed>\n- python3.14 <unfixed>\n- python3.13 <unfixed>\n- python3.11 <removed>\n- python3.9 <removed>\nhttps://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/YUHXURX2WZGKGNA4ANYBQS2VZRYQ5JNK/\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/156002\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/156003\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/f897dbf2f36a5935700b7c2d94d4681d2136b7d4 (main)\n",
                "markdown": "> When decompressing crafted zip files using the bzip/LZMA/Zstandard   compressions, Python could use an attacker-controlled size to   pre-allocate memory, possibly resulting in memory exhaustion.\n\n---\n- python3.15 <unfixed>\n- python3.14 <unfixed>\n- python3.13 <unfixed>\n- python3.11 <removed>\n- python3.9 <removed>\nhttps://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/YUHXURX2WZGKGNA4ANYBQS2VZRYQ5JNK/\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/156002\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/156003\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/commit/f897dbf2f36a5935700b7c2d94d4681d2136b7d4 (main)\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/python3.11@3.11.2-6%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                    |\n"
