            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-73283",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-73283"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-73283?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "In sshd in OpenSSH before 10.5, the restrict keyword (in authorized_keys) was supposed to be applicable to tunnel forwarding but was not.\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144192)\n[trixie] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/08/12/1\nhttps://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.5\n",
                "markdown": "> In sshd in OpenSSH before 10.5, the restrict keyword (in authorized_keys) was supposed to be applicable to tunnel forwarding but was not.\n\n---\n- openssh <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144192)\n[trixie] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/08/12/1\nhttps://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.5\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                    |\n"
              },
