            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-0992",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-0992"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-0992?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3%7Edeb12u6",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the libxml2 library. This uncontrolled resource consumption vulnerability occurs when processing XML catalogs that contain repeated <nextCatalog> elements pointing to the same downstream catalog. A remote attacker can exploit this by supplying crafted catalogs, causing the parser to redundantly traverse catalog chains. This leads to excessive CPU consumption and degrades application availability, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.2+dfsg-0.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1125696)\n[trixie] - libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-2.1+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - libxml2 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u6\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/1019\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f75abfcaa419a740a3191e56c60400f3ff18988d\nFollow-up: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/deed3b7873dff30b7f87f7f33154c9932a772522\nTests: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f8399e62a31095bf1ced01827c33f9b29494046f\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/4af23b523de5b72f27faf3e8e8a99dde5f7b82a2 (v2.15.2)\nFollow-up: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/096402c942e9d9a049f283eb4e6da431289900e1 (v2.15.2)\nTests: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f14c733327f163b49a632f03d05a58c119ed7e57 (v2.15.2)\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in the libxml2 library. This uncontrolled resource consumption vulnerability occurs when processing XML catalogs that contain repeated <nextCatalog> elements pointing to the same downstream catalog. A remote attacker can exploit this by supplying crafted catalogs, causing the parser to redundantly traverse catalog chains. This leads to excessive CPU consumption and degrades application availability, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.2+dfsg-0.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1125696)\n[trixie] - libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-2.1+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - libxml2 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u6\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/1019\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f75abfcaa419a740a3191e56c60400f3ff18988d\nFollow-up: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/deed3b7873dff30b7f87f7f33154c9932a772522\nTests: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f8399e62a31095bf1ced01827c33f9b29494046f\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/4af23b523de5b72f27faf3e8e8a99dde5f7b82a2 (v2.15.2)\nFollow-up: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/096402c942e9d9a049f283eb4e6da431289900e1 (v2.15.2)\nTests: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f14c733327f163b49a632f03d05a58c119ed7e57 (v2.15.2)\n\n|                |                                                                                                  |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u6                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u6                                                                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
