            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-27613",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-27613"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-27613?s=debian&n=git&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1%3A2.39.5-0%2Bdeb12u3",
              "help": {
                "text": "Gitk is a Tcl/Tk based Git history browser. Starting with 1.7.0, when a user clones an untrusted repository and runs gitk without additional command arguments, files for which the user has write permission can be created and truncated. The option Support per-file encoding must have been enabled before in Gitk's Preferences. This option is disabled by default. The same happens when Show origin of this line is used in the main window (regardless of whether Support per-file encoding is enabled or not). This vulnerability is fixed in 2.43.7, 2.44.4, 2.45.4, 2.46.4, 2.47.3, 2.48.2, 2.49.1, and 2.50.1.\n\n---\n- git 1:2.50.1-0.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1108983)\n[trixie] - git 1:2.47.3-0+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - git 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/git/xmqq5xg2wrd1.fsf@gitster.g/\nMerge commit: https://github.com/git/git/commit/d61cfed2c23705fbeb9c0d08f59e75ee08738950 (v2.43.7)\n",
                "markdown": "> Gitk is a Tcl/Tk based Git history browser. Starting with 1.7.0, when a user clones an untrusted repository and runs gitk without additional command arguments, files for which the user has write permission can be created and truncated. The option Support per-file encoding must have been enabled before in Gitk's Preferences. This option is disabled by default. The same happens when Show origin of this line is used in the main window (regardless of whether Support per-file encoding is enabled or not). This vulnerability is fixed in 2.43.7, 2.44.4, 2.45.4, 2.46.4, 2.47.3, 2.48.2, 2.49.1, and 2.50.1.\n\n---\n- git 1:2.50.1-0.1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1108983)\n[trixie] - git 1:2.47.3-0+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - git 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/git/xmqq5xg2wrd1.fsf@gitster.g/\nMerge commit: https://github.com/git/git/commit/d61cfed2c23705fbeb9c0d08f59e75ee08738950 (v2.43.7)\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/git@1%3A2.39.5-0%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3                                                                       |\n| Fixed version  | 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3                                                                        |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/git@1%3A2.39.5-0%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61984",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61984"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-61984?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u8",
              "help": {
                "text": "ssh in OpenSSH before 10.1 allows control characters in usernames that originate from certain possibly untrusted sources, potentially leading to code execution when a ProxyCommand is used. The untrusted sources are the command line and %-sequence expansion of a configuration file. (A configuration file that provides a complete literal username is not categorized as an untrusted source.)\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.1p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1117529)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/10/06/1\nhttps://dgl.cx/2025/10/bash-a-newline-ssh-proxycommand-cve-2025-61984\nhttps://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/35d5917652106aede47621bb3f64044604164043 (V_10_1_P1)\n",
                "markdown": "> ssh in OpenSSH before 10.1 allows control characters in usernames that originate from certain possibly untrusted sources, potentially leading to code execution when a ProxyCommand is used. The untrusted sources are the command line and %-sequence expansion of a configuration file. (A configuration file that provides a complete literal username is not categorized as an untrusted source.)\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.1p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1117529)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/10/06/1\nhttps://dgl.cx/2025/10/bash-a-newline-ssh-proxycommand-cve-2025-61984\nhttps://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/35d5917652106aede47621bb3f64044604164043 (V_10_1_P1)\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8                                                                            |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.6",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
