            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61985",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61985"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-61985?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u8",
              "help": {
                "text": "ssh in OpenSSH before 10.1 allows the '\\0' character in an ssh:// URI, potentially leading to code execution when a ProxyCommand is used.\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.1p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1117530)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u8\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/10/06/1\nhttps://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/commit/43b3bff47bb029f2299bacb6a36057981b39fdb0 (V_10_1_P1)\n",
