            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-35386",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-35386"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-35386?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u10",
              "help": {
                "text": "In OpenSSH before 10.3, command execution can occur via shell metacharacters in a username within a command line. This requires a scenario where the username on the command line is untrusted, and also requires a non-default configurations of % in ssh_config.\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.3p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1132573)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10\nhttps://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.3p1\n",
                "markdown": "> In OpenSSH before 10.3, command execution can occur via shell metacharacters in a username within a command line. This requires a scenario where the username on the command line is untrusted, and also requires a non-default configurations of % in ssh_config.\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.3p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1132573)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10\nhttps://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.3p1\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10                                                                          |\n| Fixed version  | 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10                                                                           |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
