            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55654",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-55654"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-55654?s=debian&n=openssh&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSH. This vulnerability, a heap out-of-bounds read, occurs during the cleanup of GSSAPI (Generic Security Service Application Programming Interface) indicators when a trailing NULL termination is missing in the auth-indicators array. A remote attacker, under specific configurations involving GSSAPI authentication and a Kerberos environment, could exploit this to cause the SSH authentication path to crash or abort. This leads to a denial of service (DoS), impacting the availability of the SSH service.\n\n---\n- openssh-gssapi <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1143924)\n- openssh 1:10.4p1-5\n[trixie] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2462493\nopenssh/1:10.4p1-5 dropped the GSS-API authentication and key exchange support\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in OpenSSH. This vulnerability, a heap out-of-bounds read, occurs during the cleanup of GSSAPI (Generic Security Service Application Programming Interface) indicators when a trailing NULL termination is missing in the auth-indicators array. A remote attacker, under specific configurations involving GSSAPI authentication and a Kerberos environment, could exploit this to cause the SSH authentication path to crash or abort. This leads to a denial of service (DoS), impacting the availability of the SSH service.\n\n---\n- openssh-gssapi <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1143924)\n- openssh 1:10.4p1-5\n[trixie] - openssh <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2462493\nopenssh/1:10.4p1-5 dropped the GSS-API authentication and key exchange support\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                           |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openssh@1%3A9.2p1-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-57807",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-57807"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-57807?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u4",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. ImageMagick versions lower than 14.8.2 include  insecure functions: SeekBlob(), which permits advancing the stream offset beyond the current end without increasing capacity, and WriteBlob(), which then expands by quantum + length (amortized) instead of offset + length, and copies to data + offset. When offset ≫ extent, the copy targets memory beyond the allocation, producing a deterministic heap write on 64-bit builds. No 2⁶⁴ arithmetic wrap, external delegates, or policy settings are required. This is fixed in version 14.8.2.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.3+dfsg1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1114520)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-23hg-53q6-hqfg\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/077a417a19a5ea8c85559b602754a5b928eef23e (7.1.2-3)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/ab1bb3d8ed06d0ed6aa5038b6a74aebf53af9ccf (6.9.13-29)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. ImageMagick versions lower than 14.8.2 include  insecure functions: SeekBlob(), which permits advancing the stream offset beyond the current end without increasing capacity, and WriteBlob(), which then expands by quantum + length (amortized) instead of offset + length, and copies to data + offset. When offset ≫ extent, the copy targets memory beyond the allocation, producing a deterministic heap write on 64-bit builds. No 2⁶⁴ arithmetic wrap, external delegates, or policy settings are required. This is fixed in version 14.8.2.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.3+dfsg1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1114520)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-23hg-53q6-hqfg\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/077a417a19a5ea8c85559b602754a5b928eef23e (7.1.2-3)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/ab1bb3d8ed06d0ed6aa5038b6a74aebf53af9ccf (6.9.13-29)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u4                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u4                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u4",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u4",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.8",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-14673",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-14673"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-14673?s=debian&n=postgresql-15&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C15.19-0%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Untrusted search path in PostgreSQL amcheck allows a grantee of amcheck function EXECUTE privilege to execute arbitrary functions as the owners of expression indexes that depend on the search path, via setting a hostile search path before calling the amcheck function.  Within major versions 18, 16, 15, and 14, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.  PostgreSQL 17 is unaffected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14673/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n",
                "markdown": "> Untrusted search path in PostgreSQL amcheck allows a grantee of amcheck function EXECUTE privilege to execute arbitrary functions as the owners of expression indexes that depend on the search path, via setting a hostile search path before calling the amcheck function.  Within major versions 18, 16, 15, and 14, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.  PostgreSQL 17 is unaffected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14673/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n\n|                |                                                                                                |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
