            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40386",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-40386"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-40386?s=debian&n=libexif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C0.6.24-1%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "In libexif through 0.6.25, an integer underflow in size checking for Fuji and Olympus MakerNote decoding could be used by attackers to crash or leak information out of libexif-using programs.\n\n---\n- libexif 0.6.26-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1133923)\n[trixie] - libexif 0.6.25-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libexif 0.6.24-1+deb12u1\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexif/libexif/commit/dc6eac6e9655d14d0779d99e82d0f5f442d2f34b\n",
                "markdown": "> In libexif through 0.6.25, an integer underflow in size checking for Fuji and Olympus MakerNote decoding could be used by attackers to crash or leak information out of libexif-using programs.\n\n---\n- libexif 0.6.26-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1133923)\n[trixie] - libexif 0.6.25-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libexif 0.6.24-1+deb12u1\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexif/libexif/commit/dc6eac6e9655d14d0779d99e82d0f5f442d2f34b\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libexif@0.6.24-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <0.6.24-1+deb12u1                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 0.6.24-1+deb12u1                                                                |\n"
