            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-14666",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-14666"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-14666?s=debian&n=postgresql-15&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C15.19-0%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Incomplete tracking in PostgreSQL of changes to role membership, role attributes, and database ownership allows a query to continue using cached row-level security policies after those changes require a different policy, via plan reuse.  Stale policies continue until some other event invalidates the cache or connection termination ends the session.  This permits a user to complete reads and modifications that were recently permitted but now forbidden.  An attacker must tailor an attack to a particular application's pattern of privilege removal and role-specific row security policies.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14666/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n",
                "markdown": "> Incomplete tracking in PostgreSQL of changes to role membership, role attributes, and database ownership allows a query to continue using cached row-level security policies after those changes require a different policy, via plan reuse.  Stale policies continue until some other event invalidates the cache or connection termination ends the session.  This permits a user to complete reads and modifications that were recently permitted but now forbidden.  An attacker must tailor an attack to a particular application's pattern of privilege removal and role-specific row security policies.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14666/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n\n|                |                                                                                                |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<15.19-0+deb12u1",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "15.19-0+deb12u1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-1484",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-1484"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-1484?s=debian&n=glib2.0&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.74.6-2%2Bdeb12u9",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the GLib Base64 encoding routine when processing very large input data. Due to incorrect use of integer types during length calculation, the library may miscalculate buffer boundaries. This can cause memory writes outside the allocated buffer. Applications that process untrusted or extremely large Base64 input using GLib may crash or behave unpredictably.\n\n---\n- glib2.0 2.86.3-5 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126551)\n[trixie] - glib2.0 2.84.4-3~deb13u3\n[bookworm] - glib2.0 2.74.6-2+deb12u9\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3870\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4978\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4979\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in the GLib Base64 encoding routine when processing very large input data. Due to incorrect use of integer types during length calculation, the library may miscalculate buffer boundaries. This can cause memory writes outside the allocated buffer. Applications that process untrusted or extremely large Base64 input using GLib may crash or behave unpredictably.\n\n---\n- glib2.0 2.86.3-5 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126551)\n[trixie] - glib2.0 2.84.4-3~deb13u3\n[bookworm] - glib2.0 2.74.6-2+deb12u9\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3870\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4978\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4979\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/glib2.0@2.74.6-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.74.6-2+deb12u9                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.74.6-2+deb12u9                                                                          |\n"
              },
