            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-81893",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-81893"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-81893?s=debian&n=gdk-pixbuf&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gdk-pixbuf. When loading a specially crafted JPEG image containing chunked ICC profile markers, an error during ICC profile parsing can leave stale size metadata after the profile buffer is freed. A subsequent allocation in the same decode can cause an out-of-bounds write, potentially crashing the application. To exploit this flaw, an application using gdk-pixbuf must process the malicious JPEG image.  Affected version >= 2.26.4\n\n---\n- gdk-pixbuf <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1145988)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/merge_requests/278\nIntroduced with: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/commit/4af78023ce7d3b5e3cec422a59bb4f48fa4f5886 (2.43.4)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/commit/efe658674bd103d1c9bf50809d5767a3f6dd5a01\nThe introducing commit is the fix for CVE-2025-7345.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in gdk-pixbuf. When loading a specially crafted JPEG image containing chunked ICC profile markers, an error during ICC profile parsing can leave stale size metadata after the profile buffer is freed. A subsequent allocation in the same decode can cause an out-of-bounds write, potentially crashing the application. To exploit this flaw, an application using gdk-pixbuf must process the malicious JPEG image.  Affected version >= 2.26.4\n\n---\n- gdk-pixbuf <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1145988)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/merge_requests/278\nIntroduced with: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/commit/4af78023ce7d3b5e3cec422a59bb4f48fa4f5886 (2.43.4)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdk-pixbuf/-/commit/efe658674bd103d1c9bf50809d5767a3f6dd5a01\nThe introducing commit is the fix for CVE-2025-7345.\n\n|                |                                                                                                      |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/gdk-pixbuf@2.42.10%2Bdfsg-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                                   |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                            |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/gdk-pixbuf@2.42.10%2Bdfsg-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.7",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4373",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4373"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4373?s=debian&n=glib2.0&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.74.6-2%2Bdeb12u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GLib, which is vulnerable to an integer overflow in the g_string_insert_unichar() function. When the position at which to insert the character is large, the position will overflow, leading to a buffer underwrite.\n\n---\n- glib2.0 2.84.1-3 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1104930)\n[bookworm] - glib2.0 2.74.6-2+deb12u7\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3677\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4588\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4592\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in GLib, which is vulnerable to an integer overflow in the g_string_insert_unichar() function. When the position at which to insert the character is large, the position will overflow, leading to a buffer underwrite.\n\n---\n- glib2.0 2.84.1-3 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1104930)\n[bookworm] - glib2.0 2.74.6-2+deb12u7\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/issues/3677\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4588\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/4592\n\n|                |                                                                                           |\n|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/glib2.0@2.74.6-2%2Bdeb12u5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.74.6-2+deb12u7                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.74.6-2+deb12u7                                                                          |\n"
              },
