            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18374",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18374"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-18374?s=debian&n=glibc&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Passing an effectively empty string to the `,ccs=` syntax extension of the mode argument in the `fopen` function in the GNU C Library version 2.45 or earlier may result in a heap buffer overflow when the mode string input to the function is attacker controlled.    This usage pattern is not seen in applications in common GNU/Linux distributions and applications that process user-supplied values for `ccs` should not pass them through without validation.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed>\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2026-0015\n",
                "markdown": "> Passing an effectively empty string to the `,ccs=` syntax extension of the mode argument in the `fopen` function in the GNU C Library version 2.45 or earlier may result in a heap buffer overflow when the mode string input to the function is attacker controlled.    This usage pattern is not seen in applications in common GNU/Linux distributions and applications that process user-supplied values for `ccs` should not pass them through without validation.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed>\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2026-0015\n\n|                |                                                                                       |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/glibc@2.36-9%2Bdeb12u9?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                    |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                             |\n"
