            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-34757",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-34757"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-34757?s=debian&n=libpng1.6&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1.6.39-2%2Bdeb12u5",
              "help": {
                "text": "LIBPNG is a reference library for use in applications that read, create, and manipulate PNG (Portable Network Graphics) raster image files. From 1.0.9 to before 1.6.57, passing a pointer obtained from png_get_PLTE, png_get_tRNS, or png_get_hIST back into the corresponding setter on the same png_struct/png_info pair causes the setter to read from freed memory and copy its contents into the replacement buffer. The setter frees the internal buffer before copying from the caller-supplied pointer, which now dangles. The freed region may contain stale data (producing silently corrupted chunk metadata) or data from subsequent heap allocations (leaking unrelated heap contents into the chunk struct). This vulnerability is fixed in 1.6.57.\n\n---\n- libpng1.6 1.6.57-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1133051)\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/security/advisories/GHSA-6fr7-g8h7-v645\nFixed by: https://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/398cbe3df03f4e11bb031e07f416dfdde3684e8a (v1.6.57)\nFollowup: https://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/55d20aaa322c9274491cda82c5cd4f99b48c6bcc (v1.6.57)\n",
                "markdown": "> LIBPNG is a reference library for use in applications that read, create, and manipulate PNG (Portable Network Graphics) raster image files. From 1.0.9 to before 1.6.57, passing a pointer obtained from png_get_PLTE, png_get_tRNS, or png_get_hIST back into the corresponding setter on the same png_struct/png_info pair causes the setter to read from freed memory and copy its contents into the replacement buffer. The setter frees the internal buffer before copying from the caller-supplied pointer, which now dangles. The freed region may contain stale data (producing silently corrupted chunk metadata) or data from subsequent heap allocations (leaking unrelated heap contents into the chunk struct). This vulnerability is fixed in 1.6.57.\n\n---\n- libpng1.6 1.6.57-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1133051)\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/security/advisories/GHSA-6fr7-g8h7-v645\nFixed by: https://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/398cbe3df03f4e11bb031e07f416dfdde3684e8a (v1.6.57)\nFollowup: https://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/55d20aaa322c9274491cda82c5cd4f99b48c6bcc (v1.6.57)\n\n|                |                                                                                   |\n|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libpng1.6@1.6.39-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1.6.39-2+deb12u5                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 1.6.39-2+deb12u5                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.6.39-2+deb12u5",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "1.6.39-2+deb12u5",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libpng1.6@1.6.39-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.1",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42326",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42326"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-42326?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u10",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22, when writing an IPTC output file a malicious input file could cause an out of bounds read of a single byte. This issue has been patched in versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.23+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-7wff-wpr6-vmhm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/06301590988fc62e17b4ae6e937d411cc1089ef1 (7.1.2-22)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/4bbc9cf334ec0c136d4aa8c28afab17120cc954c (6.9.13-47)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22, when writing an IPTC output file a malicious input file could cause an out of bounds read of a single byte. This issue has been patched in versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.23+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-7wff-wpr6-vmhm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/06301590988fc62e17b4ae6e937d411cc1089ef1 (7.1.2-22)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/4bbc9cf334ec0c136d4aa8c28afab17120cc954c (6.9.13-47)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u10                                                                                |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u10                                                                                 |\n"
