            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25795",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-25795"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-25795?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, in `ReadSFWImage()` (`coders/sfw.c`), when temporary file creation fails, `read_info` is destroyed before its `filename` member is accessed, causing a NULL pointer dereference and crash. Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-p33r-fqw2-rqmm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/0c7d0b9671ae2616fca106dcada45536eb4df5dc (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/b2b4f0107ba3a4427f1b5ded803c1d2cc77f2a89 (6.9.13-39)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, in `ReadSFWImage()` (`coders/sfw.c`), when temporary file creation fails, `read_info` is destroyed before its `filename` member is accessed, causing a NULL pointer dereference and crash. Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-p33r-fqw2-rqmm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/0c7d0b9671ae2616fca106dcada45536eb4df5dc (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/b2b4f0107ba3a4427f1b5ded803c1d2cc77f2a89 (6.9.13-39)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25796",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-25796"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-25796?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u8",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, in `ReadSTEGANOImage()` (`coders/stegano.c`), the `watermark` Image object is not freed on three early-return paths, resulting in a definite memory leak (~13.5KB+ per invocation) that can be exploited for denial of service. Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-g2pr-qxjg-7r2w\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/93ad259ce4f6d641eea0bee73f374af90f35efc3 (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/29aeed740553ed4e5c544e101ac468be55a919ff (6.9.13-39)\nFollowup: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/2024ae1d10a7481d04fb717b3fa9170fd294a8f3 (6.9.13-41)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, in `ReadSTEGANOImage()` (`coders/stegano.c`), the `watermark` Image object is not freed on three early-return paths, resulting in a definite memory leak (~13.5KB+ per invocation) that can be exploited for denial of service. Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-g2pr-qxjg-7r2w\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/93ad259ce4f6d641eea0bee73f374af90f35efc3 (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/29aeed740553ed4e5c544e101ac468be55a919ff (6.9.13-39)\nFollowup: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/2024ae1d10a7481d04fb717b3fa9170fd294a8f3 (6.9.13-41)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u8                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u8",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
