            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33165",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-33165"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-33165?s=debian&n=libde265&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libde265 is an open source implementation of the h.265 video codec. Prior to version 1.0.17, a crafted HEVC bitstream causes an out-of-bounds heap write confirmed by AddressSanitizer. The trigger is a stale ctb_info.log2unitSize after an SPS change where PicWidthInCtbsY and PicHeightInCtbsY stay constant but Log2CtbSizeY changes, causing set_SliceHeaderIndex to index past the allocated image metadata array and write 2 bytes past the end of a heap allocation. This issue has been patched in version 1.0.17.\n\n---\n- libde265 1.0.18-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1131468)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libde265/security/advisories/GHSA-653q-9f73-8hvg\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/commit/c7891e412106130b83f8e8ea8b7f907e9449b658 (v1.0.17)\n",
                "markdown": "> libde265 is an open source implementation of the h.265 video codec. Prior to version 1.0.17, a crafted HEVC bitstream causes an out-of-bounds heap write confirmed by AddressSanitizer. The trigger is a stale ctb_info.log2unitSize after an SPS change where PicWidthInCtbsY and PicHeightInCtbsY stay constant but Log2CtbSizeY changes, causing set_SliceHeaderIndex to index past the allocated image metadata array and write 2 bytes past the end of a heap allocation. This issue has been patched in version 1.0.17.\n\n---\n- libde265 1.0.18-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1131468)\nhttps://github.com/strukturag/libde265/security/advisories/GHSA-653q-9f73-8hvg\nFixed by: https://github.com/strukturag/libde265/commit/c7891e412106130b83f8e8ea8b7f907e9449b658 (v1.0.17)\n\n|                |                                                                                            |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libde265@1.0.11-1%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libde265@1.0.11-1%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33905",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-33905"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-33905?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u9",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. In versions below both 7.1.2-19 and 6.9.13-44, the -sample operation has an out of bounds read when an specific offset is set through the `sample:offset` define that could lead to an out of bounds read. This issue has been fixed in versions 6.9.13-44 and 7.1.2-19.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.19+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-pcvx-ph33-r5vv\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/cca607366fb38c2dde019a9088b8415ffba3a835 (7.1.2-19)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/140fc7b01fa7d870b3bc8453fb7adccfb7c1e202 (6.9.13-44)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/8d73954bf7e13a352e71a32cf7d18905577f17e8 (6.9.13-44)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. In versions below both 7.1.2-19 and 6.9.13-44, the -sample operation has an out of bounds read when an specific offset is set through the `sample:offset` define that could lead to an out of bounds read. This issue has been fixed in versions 6.9.13-44 and 7.1.2-19.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.19+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-pcvx-ph33-r5vv\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/cca607366fb38c2dde019a9088b8415ffba3a835 (7.1.2-19)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/140fc7b01fa7d870b3bc8453fb7adccfb7c1e202 (6.9.13-44)\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/8d73954bf7e13a352e71a32cf7d18905577f17e8 (6.9.13-44)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u9                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u9                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u9",
