              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to 7.1.2-21 and 6.9.13-46, a malicious MIFF file could trigger an overflow when a user opens it in the display tool and right-clicks a tile to invoke the Load / Update menu item. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.1.2-21 and 6.9.13-46.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.21+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-7mxf-ff4f-jj7p\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/25980041f145afc621233a1c050291231b627c48 (7.1.2-20)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/2b4a06cdb9b5b4b8e51247be8b38ea4cbfdfb07c (6.9.13-45)\n",
