            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59183",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59183"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-59183?s=debian&n=openexr&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. In versions 3.1.0 through 3.2.10, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13, an int32_t multiplication in OpenEXRCore's unpack_sample_table() can overflow while decoding a crafted deep tiled EXR file, producing an invalid pointer that leads to a read from an unmapped memory address and a crash. Because the overflow occurs in the standard decoding path (exr_decoding_run), any application that decodes deep tiled EXR files is affected. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-rqp5-pmwm-wj6x\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/5e55a64ad1f119a8166542f4b6e034c31b7e043a (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/a6cf183725b5665ac3fdbec640125fba5ee1ab39 (v3.3.13-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/e2adb5be3bbc3a1f82f2bc06cc9699995a99a607 (v3.2.11-rc)\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. In versions 3.1.0 through 3.2.10, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13, an int32_t multiplication in OpenEXRCore's unpack_sample_table() can overflow while decoding a crafted deep tiled EXR file, producing an invalid pointer that leads to a read from an unmapped memory address and a crash. Because the overflow occurs in the standard decoding path (exr_decoding_run), any application that decodes deep tiled EXR files is affected. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-rqp5-pmwm-wj6x\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/5e55a64ad1f119a8166542f4b6e034c31b7e043a (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/a6cf183725b5665ac3fdbec640125fba5ee1ab39 (v3.3.13-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/e2adb5be3bbc3a1f82f2bc06cc9699995a99a607 (v3.2.11-rc)\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59983",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59983"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-59983?s=debian&n=openexr&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. OpenEXR versions before 3.2.11, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13 are vulnerable on ILP32 builds to an out-of-bounds read. The vulnerability is reached when a crafted uncompressed deep-tile EXR causes the sample-count table size calculation in OpenEXRCore decoding.c to wrap before unpack_sample_table() iterates over the full attacker-controlled tile dimensions, allowing denial of service. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\n[trixie] - openexr <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-p42q-g5c9-mh9w\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/0efec58d2d28a0ee322f5028dee6fb57d459580e (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/f0e404f7298cd8563a1d30a64a1c982dbd68fc49 (v3.3.13-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/78e91146fceeee317820a146ba99a96f380945b8 (v3.2.11-rc)\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. OpenEXR versions before 3.2.11, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13 are vulnerable on ILP32 builds to an out-of-bounds read. The vulnerability is reached when a crafted uncompressed deep-tile EXR causes the sample-count table size calculation in OpenEXRCore decoding.c to wrap before unpack_sample_table() iterates over the full attacker-controlled tile dimensions, allowing denial of service. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\n[trixie] - openexr <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-p42q-g5c9-mh9w\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/0efec58d2d28a0ee322f5028dee6fb57d459580e (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/f0e404f7298cd8563a1d30a64a1c982dbd68fc49 (v3.3.13-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/78e91146fceeee317820a146ba99a96f380945b8 (v3.2.11-rc)\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59984",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-59984"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-59984?s=debian&n=openexr&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. OpenEXR versions 3.1.0 through 3.2.10, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13 are vulnerable on ILP32 builds to an out-of-bounds write. When a crafted B44-compressed scanline EXR causes the logical scratch size to truncate before allocation and uncompress_b44_impl() writes using the attacker-controlled channel width, allowing denial of service and memory corruption. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-92pq-9qv4-g68q\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/3a4214aa73041c194e450cdd6a52c0bf9f17a237 (main)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/2a7386be8ec1b637dd7c6c3b91db47a6c472ed01 (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/c550555a1657398e6a9f96c3530f8b1370a6fd94 (v3.2.11-rc)\n",
                "markdown": "> OpenEXR is the reference implementation and specification for the EXR image format, widely used in the motion picture industry. OpenEXR versions 3.1.0 through 3.2.10, 3.3.0 through 3.3.12, and 3.4.0 through 3.4.13 are vulnerable on ILP32 builds to an out-of-bounds write. When a crafted B44-compressed scanline EXR causes the logical scratch size to truncate before allocation and uncompress_b44_impl() writes using the attacker-controlled channel width, allowing denial of service and memory corruption. This issue is fixed in versions 3.2.11, 3.3.13, and 3.4.14.\n\n---\n- openexr 3.4.14-0.1\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/security/advisories/GHSA-92pq-9qv4-g68q\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/3a4214aa73041c194e450cdd6a52c0bf9f17a237 (main)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/2a7386be8ec1b637dd7c6c3b91db47a6c472ed01 (v3.4.14-rc)\nhttps://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr/commit/c550555a1657398e6a9f96c3530f8b1370a6fd94 (v3.2.11-rc)\n\n|                |                                                                                |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                             |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openexr@3.1.5-5?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
