                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4207",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4207"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-4207?s=debian&n=postgresql-15&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C15.13-0%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Buffer over-read in PostgreSQL GB18030 encoding validation allows a database input provider to achieve temporary denial of service on platforms where a 1-byte over-read can elicit process termination.  This affects the database server and also libpq.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17.5, 16.9, 15.13, 14.18, and 13.21 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-17 17.5-1\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n[bookworm] - postgresql-15 15.13-0+deb12u1\n- postgresql-13 <removed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-175-169-1513-1418-and-1321-released-3072/\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=ec5f89e8a29f32c7dbc4dd8734ed8406d771de2f (REL_17_5)\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=44ba3f55f552b56b2fbefae028fcf3ea5b53461d (REL_15_13)\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=cbadeaca9271a1bade8ef9790bae09dc92e0ed30 (REL_13_21)\n",
                "markdown": "> Buffer over-read in PostgreSQL GB18030 encoding validation allows a database input provider to achieve temporary denial of service on platforms where a 1-byte over-read can elicit process termination.  This affects the database server and also libpq.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17.5, 16.9, 15.13, 14.18, and 13.21 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-17 17.5-1\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n[bookworm] - postgresql-15 15.13-0+deb12u1\n- postgresql-13 <removed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-175-169-1513-1418-and-1321-released-3072/\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=ec5f89e8a29f32c7dbc4dd8734ed8406d771de2f (REL_17_5)\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=44ba3f55f552b56b2fbefae028fcf3ea5b53461d (REL_15_13)\nhttps://git.postgresql.org/gitweb/?p=postgresql.git;a=commit;h=cbadeaca9271a1bade8ef9790bae09dc92e0ed30 (REL_13_21)\n\n|                |                                                                                                |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <15.13-0+deb12u1                                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 15.13-0+deb12u1                                                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<15.13-0+deb12u1",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "15.13-0+deb12u1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-62171",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-62171"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-62171?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u5",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is an open source software suite for displaying, converting, and editing raster image files. In ImageMagick versions prior to 7.1.2-7 and 6.9.13-32, an integer overflow vulnerability exists in the BMP decoder on 32-bit systems. The vulnerability occurs in coders/bmp.c when calculating the extent value by multiplying image columns by bits per pixel. On 32-bit systems with size_t of 4 bytes, a malicious BMP file with specific dimensions can cause this multiplication to overflow and wrap to zero. The overflow check added to address CVE-2025-57803 is placed after the overflow occurs, making it ineffective. A specially crafted 58-byte BMP file with width set to 536,870,912 and 32 bits per pixel can trigger this overflow, causing the bytes_per_line calculation to become zero. This vulnerability only affects 32-bit builds of ImageMagick where default resource limits for width, height, and area have been manually increased beyond their defaults. 64-bit systems with size_t of 8 bytes are not vulnerable, and systems using default ImageMagick resource limits are not vulnerable. The vulnerability is fixed in versions 7.1.2-7 and 6.9.13-32.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.7+dfsg1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1118340)\n[trixie] - imagemagick 8:7.1.1.43+dfsg1-1+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - imagemagick 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-9pp9-cfwx-54rm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/cea1693e2ded51b4cc91c70c54096cbed1691c00 (7.1.2-7)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/456771fae8baa9558a1421ec8d522e6937d9b2d7 (6.9.13-32)\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is an open source software suite for displaying, converting, and editing raster image files. In ImageMagick versions prior to 7.1.2-7 and 6.9.13-32, an integer overflow vulnerability exists in the BMP decoder on 32-bit systems. The vulnerability occurs in coders/bmp.c when calculating the extent value by multiplying image columns by bits per pixel. On 32-bit systems with size_t of 4 bytes, a malicious BMP file with specific dimensions can cause this multiplication to overflow and wrap to zero. The overflow check added to address CVE-2025-57803 is placed after the overflow occurs, making it ineffective. A specially crafted 58-byte BMP file with width set to 536,870,912 and 32 bits per pixel can trigger this overflow, causing the bytes_per_line calculation to become zero. This vulnerability only affects 32-bit builds of ImageMagick where default resource limits for width, height, and area have been manually increased beyond their defaults. 64-bit systems with size_t of 8 bytes are not vulnerable, and systems using default ImageMagick resource limits are not vulnerable. The vulnerability is fixed in versions 7.1.2-7 and 6.9.13-32.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.7+dfsg1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1118340)\n[trixie] - imagemagick 8:7.1.1.43+dfsg1-1+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - imagemagick 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-9pp9-cfwx-54rm\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/cea1693e2ded51b4cc91c70c54096cbed1691c00 (7.1.2-7)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/456771fae8baa9558a1421ec8d522e6937d9b2d7 (6.9.13-32)\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u5",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-8058",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-8058"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-8058?s=debian&n=glibc&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.36-9%2Bdeb12u13",
              "help": {
                "text": "The regcomp function in the GNU C library version from 2.4 to 2.41 is  subject to a double free if some previous allocation fails. It can be  accomplished either by a malloc failure or by using an interposed malloc  that injects random malloc failures. The double free can allow buffer  manipulation depending of how the regex is constructed. This issue  affects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C library.\n\n---\n- glibc 2.41-11 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1109803)\n[bookworm] - glibc 2.36-9+deb12u13\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=33185\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob_plain;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2025-0005\nIntroduced with: https://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=commit;h=963d8d782fc98fb6dc3a66f0068795f9920c269d (glibc-2.4)\nFixed by: https://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=commit;h=7ea06e994093fa0bcca0d0ee2c1db271d8d7885d (glibc-2.42)\n",
                "markdown": "> The regcomp function in the GNU C library version from 2.4 to 2.41 is  subject to a double free if some previous allocation fails. It can be  accomplished either by a malloc failure or by using an interposed malloc  that injects random malloc failures. The double free can allow buffer  manipulation depending of how the regex is constructed. This issue  affects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C library.\n\n---\n- glibc 2.41-11 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1109803)\n[bookworm] - glibc 2.36-9+deb12u13\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=33185\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob_plain;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2025-0005\nIntroduced with: https://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=commit;h=963d8d782fc98fb6dc3a66f0068795f9920c269d (glibc-2.4)\nFixed by: https://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=commit;h=7ea06e994093fa0bcca0d0ee2c1db271d8d7885d (glibc-2.42)\n\n|                |                                                                                       |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/glibc@2.36-9%2Bdeb12u9?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.36-9+deb12u13                                                                      |\n| Fixed version  | 2.36-9+deb12u13                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.36-9+deb12u13",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "2.36-9+deb12u13",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/glibc@2.36-9%2Bdeb12u9?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-0865",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-0865"
