              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-76956?s=debian&n=expat&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "In libexpat 2.8.2 and 2.8.3 before 2.8.4, misinterpretation of getentropy's return code leads to insufficient entropy, which results in being vulnerable to hash flooding attacks, causing a denial of service via crafted XML content.\n\n---\n- expat <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144926)\n[trixie] - expat <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1326\n",
                "markdown": "> In libexpat 2.8.2 and 2.8.3 before 2.8.4, misinterpretation of getentropy's return code leads to insufficient entropy, which results in being vulnerable to hash flooding attacks, causing a denial of service via crafted XML content.\n\n---\n- expat <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144926)\n[trixie] - expat <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1326\n\n|                |                                                                                        |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/expat@2.5.0-1%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                     |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                              |\n"
