            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-56200",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-56200: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-56200?s=github&n=validator&t=npm&vr=%3C13.15.20",
              "help": {
                "text": "A URL validation bypass vulnerability exists in validator.js prior to version 13.15.20. The isURL() function uses '://' as a delimiter to parse protocols, while browsers use ':' as the delimiter. This parsing difference allows attackers to bypass protocol and domain validation by crafting URLs leading to XSS and Open Redirect attacks.\n",
                "markdown": "> A URL validation bypass vulnerability exists in validator.js prior to version 13.15.20. The isURL() function uses '://' as a delimiter to parse protocols, while browsers use ':' as the delimiter. This parsing difference allows attackers to bypass protocol and domain validation by crafting URLs leading to XSS and Open Redirect attacks.\n\n|                |                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:npm/validator@13.11.0                    |\n| Affected range | <13.15.20                                    |\n| Fixed version  | 13.15.20                                     |\n| CVSS Score     |                                          6.1 |\n| CVSS Vector    | CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<13.15.20",
                "cvssV3": 6.1,
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "fixed_version": "13.15.20",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/validator@13.11.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-64505",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-64505"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-64505?s=debian&n=libpng1.6&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1.6.39-2%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "LIBPNG is a reference library for use in applications that read, create, and manipulate PNG (Portable Network Graphics) raster image files. Prior to version 1.6.51, a heap buffer over-read vulnerability exists in libpng's png_do_quantize function when processing PNG files with malformed palette indices. The vulnerability occurs when palette_lookup array bounds are not validated against externally-supplied image data, allowing an attacker to craft a PNG file with out-of-range palette indices that trigger out-of-bounds memory access. This issue has been patched in version 1.6.51.\n\n---\n- libpng1.6 1.6.51-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1121219)\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/security/advisories/GHSA-4952-h5wq-4m42\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/pull/748\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/6a528eb5fd0dd7f6de1c39d30de0e41473431c37 (v1.6.51)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/11/22/1\n",
                "markdown": "> LIBPNG is a reference library for use in applications that read, create, and manipulate PNG (Portable Network Graphics) raster image files. Prior to version 1.6.51, a heap buffer over-read vulnerability exists in libpng's png_do_quantize function when processing PNG files with malformed palette indices. The vulnerability occurs when palette_lookup array bounds are not validated against externally-supplied image data, allowing an attacker to craft a PNG file with out-of-range palette indices that trigger out-of-bounds memory access. This issue has been patched in version 1.6.51.\n\n---\n- libpng1.6 1.6.51-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1121219)\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/security/advisories/GHSA-4952-h5wq-4m42\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/pull/748\nhttps://github.com/pnggroup/libpng/commit/6a528eb5fd0dd7f6de1c39d30de0e41473431c37 (v1.6.51)\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/11/22/1\n\n|                |                                                                                   |\n|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libpng1.6@1.6.39-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1.6.39-2+deb12u1                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 1.6.39-2+deb12u1                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.6.39-2+deb12u1",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "1.6.39-2+deb12u1",
                "purls": [
