            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18938",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18938"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-18938?s=debian&n=p11-kit&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in p11-kit. A local attacker, or one with equivalent access to a reachable RPC channel, could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability. By sending specially crafted messages, the attacker can cause the system to miscalculate memory allocation for nested attributes. This leads to a memory corruption issue, specifically a heap out-of-bounds write, which can crash the p11-kit RPC parsing process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This vulnerability is only exploitable on 32 bit systems.\n\n---\n- p11-kit 0.26.5-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144476)\n[trixie] - p11-kit <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit/pull/777\nFixed by: https://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit/commit/3e64244e538550c6a7fcf826fa8c50a4604416dc (0.26.5)\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in p11-kit. A local attacker, or one with equivalent access to a reachable RPC channel, could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability. By sending specially crafted messages, the attacker can cause the system to miscalculate memory allocation for nested attributes. This leads to a memory corruption issue, specifically a heap out-of-bounds write, which can crash the p11-kit RPC parsing process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This vulnerability is only exploitable on 32 bit systems.\n\n---\n- p11-kit 0.26.5-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1144476)\n[trixie] - p11-kit <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit/pull/777\nFixed by: https://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit/commit/3e64244e538550c6a7fcf826fa8c50a4604416dc (0.26.5)\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/p11-kit@0.24.1-2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                              |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                       |\n"
              },
