              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-12084?s=debian&n=python3.11&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C3.11.2-6%2Bdeb12u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "When building nested elements using xml.dom.minidom methods such as appendChild() that have a dependency on _clear_id_cache() the algorithm is quadratic. Availability can be impacted when building excessively nested documents.\n\n---\n- python3.14 3.14.2-1\n- python3.13 3.13.11-1\n[trixie] - python3.13 3.13.5-2+deb13u1\n- python3.11 <removed>\n[bookworm] - python3.11 3.11.2-6+deb12u7\n- python3.9 <removed>\n- python2.7 <removed>\n[bullseye] - python2.7 <end-of-life> (EOL in bullseye LTS)\n- pypy3 7.3.21+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126784)\n[trixie] - pypy3 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bookworm] - pypy3 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bullseye] - pypy3 <postponed> (Minor issue)\n- jython <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126785)\n[trixie] - jython <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bookworm] - jython <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bullseye] - jython <end-of-life> (EOL in bullseye LTS)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/142146\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/142145\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/08d8e18ad81cd45bc4a27d6da478b51ea49486e4 (main)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/027f21e417b26eed4505ac2db101a4352b7c51a0 (v3.14.2)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/ddcd2acd85d891a53e281c773b3093f9db953964 (v3.13.11)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/a46c10ec9d4050ab67b8a932e0859a2ea60c3cb8 (v3.11.15)\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/142754\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/1cc7551b3f9f71efbc88d96dce90f82de98b2454 (v3.15.0a3)\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/86747f1a1a7b4f0ea2d47fe94b841c224bae5073 (v3.13.12)\n",
                "markdown": "> When building nested elements using xml.dom.minidom methods such as appendChild() that have a dependency on _clear_id_cache() the algorithm is quadratic. Availability can be impacted when building excessively nested documents.\n\n---\n- python3.14 3.14.2-1\n- python3.13 3.13.11-1\n[trixie] - python3.13 3.13.5-2+deb13u1\n- python3.11 <removed>\n[bookworm] - python3.11 3.11.2-6+deb12u7\n- python3.9 <removed>\n- python2.7 <removed>\n[bullseye] - python2.7 <end-of-life> (EOL in bullseye LTS)\n- pypy3 7.3.21+dfsg-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126784)\n[trixie] - pypy3 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bookworm] - pypy3 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bullseye] - pypy3 <postponed> (Minor issue)\n- jython <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1126785)\n[trixie] - jython <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bookworm] - jython <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\n[bullseye] - jython <end-of-life> (EOL in bullseye LTS)\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/pull/142146\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/142145\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/08d8e18ad81cd45bc4a27d6da478b51ea49486e4 (main)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/027f21e417b26eed4505ac2db101a4352b7c51a0 (v3.14.2)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/ddcd2acd85d891a53e281c773b3093f9db953964 (v3.13.11)\nFixed by: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/a46c10ec9d4050ab67b8a932e0859a2ea60c3cb8 (v3.11.15)\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/142754\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/1cc7551b3f9f71efbc88d96dce90f82de98b2454 (v3.15.0a3)\nRegression: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/86747f1a1a7b4f0ea2d47fe94b841c224bae5073 (v3.13.12)\n\n|                |                                                                                              |\n|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        |