            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39615",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39615"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-39615?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3%7Edeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "Xmlsoft Libxml2 v2.11.0 was discovered to contain an out-of-bounds read via the xmlSAX2StartElement() function at /libxml2/SAX2.c. This vulnerability allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via supplying a crafted XML file. NOTE: the vendor's position is that the product does not support the legacy SAX1 interface with custom callbacks; there is a crash even without crafted input.\n\n---\n[experimental] - libxml2 2.12.3+dfsg-0exp1\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1051230)\n[buster] - libxml2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/535\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d0c3f01e110d54415611c5fa0040cdf4a56053f9 (v2.12.0)\nFollowup: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/235b15a590eecf97b09e87bdb7e4f8333e9de129 (v2.12.0)\n",
                "markdown": "> Xmlsoft Libxml2 v2.11.0 was discovered to contain an out-of-bounds read via the xmlSAX2StartElement() function at /libxml2/SAX2.c. This vulnerability allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via supplying a crafted XML file. NOTE: the vendor's position is that the product does not support the legacy SAX1 interface with custom callbacks; there is a crash even without crafted input.\n\n---\n[experimental] - libxml2 2.12.3+dfsg-0exp1\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1051230)\n[buster] - libxml2 <no-dsa> (Minor issue)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/535\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d0c3f01e110d54415611c5fa0040cdf4a56053f9 (v2.12.0)\nFollowup: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/235b15a590eecf97b09e87bdb7e4f8333e9de129 (v2.12.0)\n\n|                |                                                                                                  |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45322",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45322"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-45322?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3%7Edeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "libxml2 through 2.11.5 has a use-after-free that can only occur after a certain memory allocation fails. This occurs in xmlUnlinkNode in tree.c. NOTE: the vendor's position is \"I don't think these issues are critical enough to warrant a CVE ID ... because an attacker typically can't control when memory allocations fail.\"\n\n---\n[experimental] - libxml2 2.12.3+dfsg-0exp1\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1053629)\n[buster] - libxml2 <postponed> (Minor issue, very hard/unlikely to trigger)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/583\nOriginally fixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d39f78069dff496ec865c73aa44d7110e429bce9 (v2.12.0)\nIntroduced regression (and thus commit reverted temporarily upstream):\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/634\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/30d7660ba87c8487b26582ccc050f4d2880ccb3c (v2.12.2)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/8707838e69f9c6e729c1d1d46bb3681d9e622be5 (v2.13.0)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/344\nhttp://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2023/10/06/5\n",
                "markdown": "> libxml2 through 2.11.5 has a use-after-free that can only occur after a certain memory allocation fails. This occurs in xmlUnlinkNode in tree.c. NOTE: the vendor's position is \"I don't think these issues are critical enough to warrant a CVE ID ... because an attacker typically can't control when memory allocations fail.\"\n\n---\n[experimental] - libxml2 2.12.3+dfsg-0exp1\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1053629)\n[buster] - libxml2 <postponed> (Minor issue, very hard/unlikely to trigger)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/583\nOriginally fixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/d39f78069dff496ec865c73aa44d7110e429bce9 (v2.12.0)\nIntroduced regression (and thus commit reverted temporarily upstream):\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/634\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/30d7660ba87c8487b26582ccc050f4d2880ccb3c (v2.12.2)\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/8707838e69f9c6e729c1d1d46bb3681d9e622be5 (v2.13.0)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/344\nhttp://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2023/10/06/5\n\n|                |                                                                                                  |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
