            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-25982",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-25982"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-25982?s=debian&n=imagemagick&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability exists in the `coders/dcm.c` module. When processing DICOM files with a specific configuration, the decoder loop incorrectly reads bytes per iteration. This causes the function to read past the end of the allocated buffer, potentially leading to a Denial of Service (crash) or Information Disclosure (leaking heap memory into the image). Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-pmq6-8289-hx3v\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/4e1f5381d4ccbb6b71927e94c5d257fa883b3af7 (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/b4c37614b6da7695cb4f5b3c6e326a37bdf2b1a9 (6.9.13-39)\nfor imagemagick6 fix in included in a jumbo security patch with other fix like CVE-2026-25797\n",
                "markdown": "> ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability exists in the `coders/dcm.c` module. When processing DICOM files with a specific configuration, the decoder loop incorrectly reads bytes per iteration. This causes the function to read past the end of the allocated buffer, potentially leading to a Denial of Service (crash) or Information Disclosure (leaking heap memory into the image). Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.15+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-pmq6-8289-hx3v\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/4e1f5381d4ccbb6b71927e94c5d257fa883b3af7 (7.1.2-14)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/b4c37614b6da7695cb4f5b3c6e326a37bdf2b1a9 (6.9.13-39)\nfor imagemagick6 fix in included in a jumbo security patch with other fix like CVE-2026-25797\n\n|                |                                                                                                               |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick@8%3A6.9.11.60%2Bdfsg-1.6%2Bdeb12u2?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7                                                                                 |\n| Fixed version  | 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.6+deb12u7",
