              "help": {
                "text": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-16 and 6.9.13-41, A heap-buffer-overflow vulnerability exists in the PCL encode due to an undersized output buffer allocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.1.2-16 and 6.9.13-41.\n\n---\n- imagemagick 8:7.1.2.16+dfsg1-1\nhttps://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-467j-76j7-5885\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/d622bd6023310d57cec1e8f265095a1979210371 (7.1.2-16)\nFixed by: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/6a602fb36f181a0089848344a3b0d79fc6155a2b (6.9.13-41)\nfor imagemagick6 fixed in a jumbo patch\n",
