            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32775",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32775"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-32775?s=debian&n=libexif&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C0.6.24-1%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "libexif through 0.6.25 has a flaw in decoding MakerNotes. If the exif_mnote_data_get_value function gets passed in a 0 size, the passed in-buffer would be overwritten due to an integer underflow.\n\n---\n- libexif 0.6.26-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1131116)\n[trixie] - libexif 0.6.25-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libexif 0.6.24-1+deb12u1\nhttps://github.com/libexif/libexif/issues/247\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexif/libexif/commit/7df372e9d31d7c993a22b913c813a5f7ec4f3692\n",
                "markdown": "> libexif through 0.6.25 has a flaw in decoding MakerNotes. If the exif_mnote_data_get_value function gets passed in a 0 size, the passed in-buffer would be overwritten due to an integer underflow.\n\n---\n- libexif 0.6.26-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1131116)\n[trixie] - libexif 0.6.25-1+deb13u1\n[bookworm] - libexif 0.6.24-1+deb12u1\nhttps://github.com/libexif/libexif/issues/247\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexif/libexif/commit/7df372e9d31d7c993a22b913c813a5f7ec4f3692\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libexif@0.6.24-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <0.6.24-1+deb12u1                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 0.6.24-1+deb12u1                                                                |\n"
