              "help": {
                "text": "In OpenSSH before 10.3, a file downloaded by scp may be installed setuid or setgid, an outcome contrary to some users' expectations, if the download is performed as root with -O (legacy scp protocol) and without -p (preserve mode).\n\n---\n- openssh 1:10.3p1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1132572)\n[trixie] - openssh 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u3\n[bookworm] - openssh 1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10\nhttps://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.3p1\n",
