            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56171",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-56171"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-56171?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3%7Edeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "libxml2 before 2.12.10 and 2.13.x before 2.13.6 has a use-after-free in xmlSchemaIDCFillNodeTables and xmlSchemaBubbleIDCNodeTables in xmlschemas.c. To exploit this, a crafted XML document must be validated against an XML schema with certain identity constraints, or a crafted XML schema must be used.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-0.4 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098320)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/828\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/2\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/5880a9a6bd97c0f9ac8fc4f30110fe023f484746\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/245b70d7d2768572ae1b05b3668ca858b9ec4ed4 (v2.12.10)\n",
                "markdown": "> libxml2 before 2.12.10 and 2.13.x before 2.13.6 has a use-after-free in xmlSchemaIDCFillNodeTables and xmlSchemaBubbleIDCNodeTables in xmlschemas.c. To exploit this, a crafted XML document must be validated against an XML schema with certain identity constraints, or a crafted XML schema must be used.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-0.4 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098320)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/828\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/2\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/5880a9a6bd97c0f9ac8fc4f30110fe023f484746\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/245b70d7d2768572ae1b05b3668ca858b9ec4ed4 (v2.12.10)\n\n|                |                                                                                                  |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-24855",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-24855"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-24855?s=debian&n=libxslt&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C1.1.35-1%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "numbers.c in libxslt before 1.1.43 has a use-after-free because, in nested XPath evaluations, an XPath context node can be modified but never restored. This is related to xsltNumberFormatGetValue, xsltEvalXPathPredicate, xsltEvalXPathStringNs, and xsltComputeSortResultInternal.\n\n---\n- libxslt 1.1.35-1.2 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1100566)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxslt/-/issues/128\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxslt/-/commit/c7c7f1f78dd202a053996fcefe57eb994aec8ef2 (v1.1.43)\n",
                "markdown": "> numbers.c in libxslt before 1.1.43 has a use-after-free because, in nested XPath evaluations, an XPath context node can be modified but never restored. This is related to xsltNumberFormatGetValue, xsltEvalXPathPredicate, xsltEvalXPathStringNs, and xsltComputeSortResultInternal.\n\n---\n- libxslt 1.1.35-1.2 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1100566)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxslt/-/issues/128\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxslt/-/commit/c7c7f1f78dd202a053996fcefe57eb994aec8ef2 (v1.1.43)\n\n|                |                                                                                 |\n|----------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxslt@1.1.35-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <1.1.35-1+deb12u1                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 1.1.35-1+deb12u1                                                                |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.1.35-1+deb12u1",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "1.1.35-1+deb12u1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libxslt@1.1.35-1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-24928",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-24928"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-24928?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3%7Edeb12u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "libxml2 before 2.12.10 and 2.13.x before 2.13.6 has a stack-based buffer overflow in xmlSnprintfElements in valid.c. To exploit this, DTD validation must occur for an untrusted document or untrusted DTD. NOTE: this is similar to CVE-2017-9047.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-0.4 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098321)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/847\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/2\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/8c8753ad5280ee13aee5eec9b0f6eee2ed920f57\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/858ca26c0689161a6b903a6682cc8a1cc10a0ea8 (v2.12.10)\n",
                "markdown": "> libxml2 before 2.12.10 and 2.13.x before 2.13.6 has a stack-based buffer overflow in xmlSnprintfElements in valid.c. To exploit this, DTD validation must occur for an untrusted document or untrusted DTD. NOTE: this is similar to CVE-2017-9047.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.12.7+dfsg+really2.9.14-0.4 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1098321)\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/issues/847\nhttps://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2025/02/18/2\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/8c8753ad5280ee13aee5eec9b0f6eee2ed920f57\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/858ca26c0689161a6b903a6682cc8a1cc10a0ea8 (v2.12.10)\n\n|                |                                                                                                  |\n|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.9.14%2Bdfsg-1.3~deb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                         |\n| Fixed version  | 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2                                                                          |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u2",
