            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-63388",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-63388"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-63388?s=debian&n=libevent&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Libevent is an event notification library. Prior to 2.1.13 and 2.2.2-alpha, libevent has a heap out-of-bounds write in bufferevent_sock.c when bufferevent_socket_set_conn_address_ copies a kernel-supplied AF_UNIX peer address into bufferevent_private.conn_address. Release builds compiled with NDEBUG disable the EVUTIL_ASSERT length guard, and the evhttp accept path can pass a 110-byte sockaddr from accept() into the 28-byte field. An unauthenticated local peer able to connect to an AF_UNIX listener can overwrite the adjacent dns_request pointer and heap data, causing memory corruption with confidentiality, integrity, and availability impact. This issue is fixed in versions 2.1.13 and 2.2.2-alpha.\n\n---\n- libevent 2.1.13-stable-1\nhttps://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-cvq5-vrvr-j338\nFixed by: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/ef38f926e9cd1f082416c6fff13587bc1f431d72 (release-2.1.13-stable)\nFixed by: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/52057cb33d0c20c0a0453fbabe6c0c96854931b9 (release-2.2.2-alpha)\n",
                "markdown": "> Libevent is an event notification library. Prior to 2.1.13 and 2.2.2-alpha, libevent has a heap out-of-bounds write in bufferevent_sock.c when bufferevent_socket_set_conn_address_ copies a kernel-supplied AF_UNIX peer address into bufferevent_private.conn_address. Release builds compiled with NDEBUG disable the EVUTIL_ASSERT length guard, and the evhttp accept path can pass a 110-byte sockaddr from accept() into the 28-byte field. An unauthenticated local peer able to connect to an AF_UNIX listener can overwrite the adjacent dns_request pointer and heap data, causing memory corruption with confidentiality, integrity, and availability impact. This issue is fixed in versions 2.1.13 and 2.2.2-alpha.\n\n---\n- libevent 2.1.13-stable-1\nhttps://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-cvq5-vrvr-j338\nFixed by: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/ef38f926e9cd1f082416c6fff13587bc1f431d72 (release-2.1.13-stable)\nFixed by: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/52057cb33d0c20c0a0453fbabe6c0c96854931b9 (release-2.2.2-alpha)\n\n|                |                                                                                         |\n|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/libevent@2.1.12-stable-8?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | >0                                                                                      |\n| Fixed version  | not fixed                                                                               |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libevent@2.1.12-stable-8?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.4",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
