            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-14677",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-14677"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-14677?s=debian&n=postgresql-15&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=12&vr=%3C15.19-0%2Bdeb12u1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Integer wraparound in PostgreSQL 32-bit builds of pltcl and plperl allows an object creator to cause the server to undersize an allocation and write out-of-bounds via crafted function bodies.  This may execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the database.  CVE-2026-6473 had fixed similar problems.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14677/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n",
                "markdown": "> Integer wraparound in PostgreSQL 32-bit builds of pltcl and plperl allows an object creator to cause the server to undersize an allocation and write out-of-bounds via crafted function bodies.  This may execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the database.  CVE-2026-6473 had fixed similar problems.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.5, 17.11, 16.15, 15.19, and 14.24 are affected.\n\n---\n- postgresql-18 18.6-1\n- postgresql-17 <removed>\n- postgresql-15 <removed>\n- postgresql-13 <unfixed>\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/support/security/CVE-2026-14677/\nhttps://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-186-1711-1615-1519-1424-and-19-beta-3-released-3365/\n\n|                |                                                                                                |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Package        | pkg:deb/debian/postgresql-15@15.10-0%2Bdeb12u1?os_distro=bookworm&os_name=debian&os_version=12 |\n| Affected range | <15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                               |\n| Fixed version  | 15.19-0+deb12u1                                                                                |\n"
              },
